    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Type 2 diabetes often develops slowly and can cause no noticeable symptoms in its early stages. When warning signs do appear, they are usually mild at first and include:",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "no noticeable symptoms in its early stages"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Increased thirst and frequent urination: High blood sugar forces your kidneys to work harder to filter and absorb excess glucose, causing you to pee more often (especially at night) and leave you feeling constantly thirsty.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Persistent fatigue: Because your cells cannot properly take in glucose to use as energy, you may feel unusually tired, sluggish, or drained even after resting.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Increased hunger: Even after eating, you may feel constantly hungry because your body is unable to move sugar from your blood into your cells for fuel.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Blurred vision: Fluctuating blood sugar levels can cause fluid to shift inside the lenses of your eyes, making it difficult for them to focus.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Slow-healing cuts or sores: High blood sugar impairs your circulation and weakens your immune response, making minor injuries take much longer to heal.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              8,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Frequent infections: You may notice more frequent urinary tract infections (UTIs), skin infections, or yeast infections.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tingling or numbness: Mild nerve damage (neuropathy) can cause a pins-and-needles sensation, pain, or numbness in your hands or feet.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              11
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Darkened skin patches: Velvety, dark patches of skin (acanthosis nigricans), most commonly found in the folds of the neck, armpits, or groin, can be an early sign of insulin resistance ."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4,
          11
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How It Is Diagnosed"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Because early symptoms are often subtle or completely absent, a simple blood test is the only reliable way to know if you have type 2 diabetes or prediabetes. Common diagnostic tests provided through resources like the Mayo Clinic include:",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Mayo Clinic",
            "link": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/type-2-diabetes/symptoms-causes/syc-20351193"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          11,
          12
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "HbA1c test: Measures your average blood sugar level over the past two to three months."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fasting plasma glucose test: Measures your blood sugar after an overnight fast."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Random blood glucose test: Measures your blood sugar at any time of day regardless of when you last ate."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          13,
          14,
          15
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What specific symptoms or changes you've noticed"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you have risk factors like family history or age over 45"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you understand when to talk to a doctor about getting screened ."
      }
    ],
